Proposition 2 (a legislatively referred constitutional amendment) would raise the cap on California’s Budget Stabilization Account (“rainy day fund”) from 10% to 20% of General Fund tax revenues, require larger deposits in high-revenue years, extend extra debt payments through 2040, and adjust how reserves interact with the Gann spending limit. It needs a simple majority to pass. Pre-election forecasts (as of November 2) projected roughly 62–63% Yes.[[2]](https://onpointpolitics.us/forecast/measures/ca/proposition-2)

